<%#
  locals: path:, title:, subtitle:, aside: (captured html, right-hand value - a date, or a total + badge),
          call: nil ({ phone:, name: } - adds a tap-to-call button beside the row)

  One dashboard preview row. A list item rather than a table row: the cards are narrow at every
  width (a third of the page on desktop, the full phone width on site), and a 3-4 column table
  squeezed into them pushed the money column off-card behind a scroll with no visible cue. The
  whole row is the link, so the tap target is the full row, not just the title text. The call
  button sits beside that link rather than inside it (a link can't contain another link).
%>
<% call = local_assigns[:call] %>
<li class="@container flex items-stretch">
  <%# In a narrow row the value stacks under the title instead of beside it: a badge or date
      plus the call button took ~170px of a 375px row and cut titles to one word. The switch is
      a container query on the row (@md = 28rem), not a viewport breakpoint - a half-width card
      at 1024px is as narrow as a phone. %>
  <%= link_to path, class: "flex flex-1 min-w-0 flex-col gap-1 @md:flex-row @md:items-center @md:justify-between @md:gap-4 min-h-11 py-3 pl-6 #{call ? "pr-2" : "pr-6"} hover:bg-base-content/[0.04] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary" do %>
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <%# Two lines before clipping, not one: similar titles ("Kitchen Renovation — Mitchell
          Residence") differ at the end, which single-line truncation hides on a phone. %>
      <p class="font-medium text-base-content line-clamp-2"><%= title %></p>
      <p class="text-base-content/70 truncate"><%= subtitle %></p>
    </div>
    <%# flex-wrap in a narrow row lays a total and its badge side by side under the title;
        @md:block restores their stacked, right-aligned form. %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 @md:block @md:shrink-0 @md:text-right tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap"><%= aside %></div>
  <% end %>
  <% if call %>
    <%# pl-2 leaves a gap between the row link's hit area and the call button's, so a thumb
        aimed at one doesn't land on the other. %>
    <div class="flex items-center pl-2 pr-4">
      <%= render "shared/call_button", phone: call[:phone], name: call[:name] %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</li>
